problem_text:
Find all functions $f:\mathbb{Z}_{\ge 0}\times\mathbb{Z}_{\ge 0}\to\mathbb{Z}_{\ge 0}$ such that for every $m,n\ge 0$ the following hold:

(i) $f(m,0)=f(0,n)=1$;

(ii) $f(m,n)=f(m-1,n)+f(m,n-1)+f(m-1,n-1)$ (with the convention that the terms on the right are defined only when the indices are non‑negative);

(iii) the exponential generating function satisfies
\[\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{f(m,n)x^{m}y^{n}}{m!\,n!}=\exp\bigl(x+y+xy\bigr).\]
Determine $f(m,n)$ for all $m,n$.

